Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: runsuite.c
Line: 135
Function: initializeLibxml2
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: xmlXPathNewContext(NULL) can fail and return NULL on allocation failure, but the result is dereferenced immediately without a NULL check (ctxtXPath->cache). This leads to a NULL pointer dereference if allocation fails. Subsequent calls using ctxtXPath (e.g., xmlXPathRegisterNs) would also dereference NULL.

